 {"type":"failure","classification":"tactical","recorded_at":"2026-08-22T18:08:57.202Z","evidence":{"commit":"423d296789e3a8c6f97e29e6f03f4fe41fb56356"},"description":"A previous implementer pass left a compiled 'gofib' binary in the worktree root (gitignored, so the gate stayed green). Hard rule: build smoke checks must not leave binaries behind — use 'go run .' (builds to cache) or build into a temp dir outside the worktree, and remove any stray binary before finishing the pass.","resolution":"Binary removed with 'rm -f gofib'; smoke checks now use 'go run .' which builds into the Go cache and never touches the worktree.","id":"mx-a58327"}
